---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import { CommandComposer, CommandPalette, CommandPlayground, CommandProjects } from '../../components/CommandDemo';
---

<Docs title="Command" description="Searchable lists of actions and choices for pickers and command palettes.">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Command</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A search field over a list of actions or choices. Type to filter, move with the arrow keys, and press Enter to
    choose. Put it inline, inside a popover picker, or in a command palette dialog.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8" id="command-demo">
    <CommandPlayground client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Command usage"
      code={`import {
  Command,
  CommandEmpty,
  CommandGroup,
  CommandInput,
  CommandItem,
  CommandList,
  CommandSeparator,
  CommandShortcut,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/command";

<Command>
  <CommandInput aria-label="Search sample commands" placeholder="Search sample commands…" />
  <CommandList>
    <CommandEmpty>No matching commands.</CommandEmpty>
    <CommandGroup heading="Suggestions">
      <CommandItem onSelect={newDraft}>
        <Plus size={16} aria-hidden="true" />
        New draft
        <CommandShortcut>⌘ N</CommandShortcut>
      </CommandItem>
      <CommandItem onSelect={openFolder}>
        <Folder size={16} aria-hidden="true" />
        Open folder
      </CommandItem>
    </CommandGroup>
    <CommandSeparator />
    <CommandGroup heading="Settings">
      <CommandItem disabled>Unavailable action</CommandItem>
    </CommandGroup>
  </CommandList>
</Command>`}
    />
    <p>
      Give the input an <code>aria-label</code> or pass <code>label</code> to <code>Command</code>. Each item matches on
      its text unless you pass a <code>value</code>, and <code>onSelect</code> receives that value. Groups and
      separators hide while nothing in them matches.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="command-palette">
    <h2 class="section-title">Command palette</h2>
    <p>
      <code>CommandDialog</code> pins a Command near the top of the screen in a 24rem dialog. Its <code>title</code> and{' '}
      <code>description</code> are visually hidden but announced. Escape closes it; add <code>showCloseButton</code> for
      a corner close button. Wire your own shortcut such as ⌘K to open it.
    </p>
    <CommandPalette client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="command-composer">
    <h2 class="section-title">Pickers in a popover</h2>
    <p>
      Put a Command in <code>PopoverContent size="menu"</code> or <code>size="picker"</code>; both have no padding, so
      the search and list run edge to edge. Set <code>data-checked</code> on the current item to show a trailing check.
      Use a long <code>value</code> such as label plus description so both are searchable. Content after{' '}
      <code>Command</code>, such as an effort setting, stays outside the list.
    </p>
    <CommandComposer client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="command-projects">
    <h2 class="section-title">Controlled search and list states</h2>
    <p>
      Pass <code>value</code> and <code>onValueChange</code> to <code>CommandInput</code> to clear the search when the
      popover closes or from a button in <code>CommandEmpty</code>. When an item's <code>value</code> is an id, pass its
      name in <code>keywords</code> so it still matches. Show loading, error with retry, and empty-workspace notes as
      siblings after <code>CommandList</code>.
    </p>
    <CommandProjects client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="command-api">
    <h2 class="section-title">API</h2>
    <p>
      <code>Command</code> is a <code>div</code> that owns the search and the active item. It takes <code>label</code>,{' '}
      <code>loop</code> (wrap at the ends), <code>shouldFilter</code> (set <code>false</code> to filter items yourself),
      and <code>filter(value, search, keywords)</code>, which returns a score where <code>0</code> hides the item.
      Matches are ranked: prefix, then word start, then substring, then letters in order. The default is exported as{' '}
      <code>defaultCommandFilter</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>CommandInput</code> takes input props plus controlled <code>value</code> and <code>onValueChange</code>, and
      forwards <code>ref</code>. <code>CommandList</code> scrolls at 18rem. <code>CommandEmpty</code> renders only when
      nothing matches.
      <code>CommandGroup</code> takes an optional <code>heading</code> and <code>forceMount</code>.{' '}
      <code>CommandSeparator</code> hides while searching unless <code>alwaysRender</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>CommandItem</code> takes <code>value</code>, <code>keywords</code>, <code>disabled</code>,{' '}
      <code>onSelect</code>, <code>forceMount</code>, and <code>data-checked</code>. <code>CommandShortcut</code> is a
      trailing hint and replaces the check. <code>CommandDialog</code> takes the Dialog root props plus{' '}
      <code>title</code>, <code>description</code>, <code>showCloseButton</code>, <code>closeLabel</code>,{' '}
      <code>container</code>, and <code>className</code>. Every part sets a <code>data-slot</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The input is a <code>combobox</code> that controls the <code>listbox</code>. Focus stays in the input and the
      active option is announced through <code>aria-activedescendant</code>. Arrow keys move, Home and End jump to the
      ends, ⌘ or Ctrl with arrows jumps to the first or last item, Alt with arrows jumps between groups, Ctrl+N and
      Ctrl+P also move, and Enter chooses. Disabled items are skipped. Buttons inside the Command, such as Clear search,
      keep their own keys.
    </p>
    <p>
      When nothing matches, the list drops its <code>listbox</code> role, the input reports{' '}
      <code>aria-expanded="false"</code>, and the empty message and its actions read as ordinary content. Separators are
      decorative and hidden from assistive technology.
    </p>
    <p>
      Highlight and check changes fade over 120ms and stop when reduced motion is requested. In forced-colors mode the
      active item gets an outline.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Command uses <code>--sprout-surface</code>, <code>--sprout-text</code>, <code>--sprout-muted</code>,{' '}
      <code>--sprout-line</code>, <code>--sprout-input</code>, <code>--sprout-hover</code>, <code>--sprout-focus</code>,
      and the control and panel radii. It needs no brand color, so it looks the same with the neutral and TulipFarm
      themes in light and dark mode.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
